Spec: Spec Kit × SpecDD Integration Lab

Platform: Node.js 22+/Spec Kit 1.0.7/SpecDD 1.5

Purpose:
  Provide a local integration lab for a thin bridge that projects SpecDD system authority into the Spec Kit change lifecycle without forking, merging, or duplicating either system.

Structure:
  ./README.md: User-facing project overview, installation, concepts, and normal usage
  ./integration: Bridge extension and Spec Kit preset source
  ./fixtures: Integration-test systems used to exercise authority behavior
  ./docs: Project specification, implementation plan, and development guidance
  ./scripts: Repository bootstrap tooling

Owns:
  Repository-wide bridge architecture and source/generated-state separation.
  ./dev-scripts.include
  ./docs/TODO.md
  ./integration/**/.gitkeep
  ./fixtures/**/.gitkeep
  ./HUMAN-REQUEST*.md

References:
  ./docs/spec.md
  ./docs/development.md

Must:
  Spec Kit remains authoritative for the change lifecycle and SpecDD remains authoritative for persistent system semantics.
  Bridge-derived state remains reconstructible from canonical Spec Kit and SpecDD artifacts.
  Integration source remains separate from generated or installed upstream state.
  Compatibility pins stay at Spec Kit `1.0.7`, SpecDD CLI `1.1.1`, and SpecDD framework `1.5` until a deliberate compatibility task changes them.

Must not:
  Patch files under `.specify/`, `.specify-agent/`, or `.specdd/` to implement bridge behavior.
  Maintain a second persistent copy of SpecDD constraints in Spec Kit feature artifacts.
